From cc2f1e51f046d3687e6611437dc2a9f73770a640 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:31:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: the limit of PCM to the display is not lost in a
 change of mode

Since "AudioEngine: PCM in no more channels than the display takes" the
channels of PCM follow the audio data of the display (its ELD), read when
the outputs are listed. A test of 2026-10-21 (an LG C5 on the HDMI output
of the integrated graphics, Raphael, amdgpu; the TV declared PCM in 2
channels, "Number of channels" was 7.1) shows the limit lost for a whole
film: the sink opened 2 channels for a DTS 5.1 track, the outputs were
listed again right after, in the change of mode to the video, while the
HDA HDMI codec had no valid ELD of the TV ("m_display: none", every
channel of ALSA's maps), the sink opened 6 channels, and nothing listed
the outputs again: the film went out in 5.1 PCM to a TV that takes 2.
The same happened when the film stopped. On the NVIDIA card of the same
PC one listing out of eleven of another start fell in a change of mode
as well, and the next listing, 28 s later, healed it.

Two reasons, from the code:

- amdgpu tells the audio driver that the audio of an output is gone and
  that it is back in the commit that sets a mode
  (amdgpu_dm_commit_audio()); each is a change of the ELD control, which
  Kodi takes as a device change. A device change that came while the
  engine had the sink suspended for a lost display (between DISPLAYLOST
  and DISPLAYRESET) was dropped, and a display reset opens the sink again
  without listing the outputs. Around the two changes of mode for Dolby
  Vision of that start no listing was made at all; the snapshot of the
  diagnostics after them found the ELD of the TV valid. In which order
  the two changes reached Kodi in the change of mode to the DTS film is
  not in the log.
- a listing that falls between the two finds no audio data, and the
  limit was then taken away (0, not known).

Now a device change while the sink is suspended for a lost display is
kept, and at the display reset the outputs are listed again, and the
settings loaded, before the sink is opened (logged: "the outputs changed
while the display was being reset: they are listed again"); a reset
without such a change costs nothing more than before. And while the
display of an output has no audio data, the engine takes the last ones
read from a display of that output in this run
(AE::PCM::KeepWhileAway()); a display that is there gives what it says,
also nothing. The log line of the limit says when they are the kept
ones. An output whose display never had audio data in this run is not
limited, as before.

Not changed: what a listing in the middle of a change of mode says of
whether a display is there, which the audio output that follows the
display reads too: on the PC of the user no output was followed in that
listing (every HDMI output said "none").

Host tests (TestAEPcmChannels): the listings of that start, with the
ELD of the TV, give 2.0 at each one, and the limit follows a display
that is there; with the code before (what was read, always) and two more
mutations they fail. The state machine is not run on the host: compiled,
and read.
